unknown subcommand does, and does nothing.

  mode        Prints ONE line, `index` or `primary`, from the configuration
              alone: it opens no database. No configuration file, or no
              `mode=`, is `index`. A configuration it refuses is 2.
  register    The writers' snapshot and commit, `register classify`'s one
              classifier, and the readers' and the guard's `register read`.
  journal     The in-doubt lookup by write id; `--since` and `--last` read.
  render      `--images`, the render set at a seq; `--checkout`, the renderer
              fork; `--revert <sha>`, S2's way out of a divergence that
              journals an entry with no edits naming the stray, then renders.
  import, cutover, rollback, outage
              The operator's acts (operations.md sections 2.2 to 2.5), each
              from the operator lane's own checkout. `import --single <sha>`
              and `render --revert <sha>` are S2's two ways out of a
              divergence: see `{PROG} import --single --help`.
  bootstrap, login, ready, set-mode
              The operator tools (operations.md section 2.4).
  serve       The register service (SVC-3), on `mode=primary` only.

  While this build refuses `mode=primary` (Q6(c): the renderer's git half is
